# Partner Check Overview

Flutter mobile app (iOS/Android) for comparing contact "compatibility" via phone-number-derived colors in dual side-by-side panes.

## Stack

- **State**: `setState` in screens; `Provider` only for `ProSubscriptionService` (IAP)
- **Persistence**: `SharedPreferences` via `ContactStorageService`
- **Contacts**: `flutter_contacts` + `permission_handler`
- **l10n**: Hand-maintained `AppLocalizations` (not `flutter gen-l10n`)
- **Lint**: `package:flutter_lints/flutter.yaml`

## Layout

```
lib/screens/   — UI + most state (contacts_page.dart is large; prefer targeted edits)
lib/services/  — persistence, permissions, IAP
lib/widgets/   — presentational components with callbacks
lib/utils/     — static helpers (color, match, phone, pro gate, RTL)
lib/models.dart — StoredContact only
lib/l10n/      — app_localizations.dart + 17 .arb files
```

## Core domain

- Color from last 6 phone digits → hex (`PhoneUtils`, `ColorUtils`)
- Match = hue within ~30° (`MatchCalculator`)
- Free tier: 10 contacts; bulk import requires Pro (`pro_gate.dart`)
- Self-contact: Android auto-detects profile; iOS requires manual pick (`SelfContactFinder`)

## Agent scope

- This is a **Flutter/Dart** project — ignore Svelte/shadcn rules
- Prefer minimal diffs; match existing naming and patterns
- Platform splits use `dart:io` `Platform.isAndroid` / `Platform.isIOS`
